# November 28, 2026: Spokane, Washington (region wa). The names came from one video about the city's old buildings
# (Old World Exploration, 2022), taken as tips only: every fact below is from a source opened for this batch.
# Sixteen standing places, nearly all downtown and on Riverside Avenue: the Masonic Temple, the Elks Temple and the
# Spokane Club on the Riverside Avenue Historic District's row of colonnades, the Catholic cathedral of Our Lady of
# Lourdes, the Episcopal cathedral of St. John, St. Aloysius at Gonzaga, the county courthouse, the federal building,
# the Davenport Hotel, the Review, Empire State, Old National Bank and Paulsen buildings, the Monroe Street Bridge, the
# Great Northern clock tower and the old Holy Names Academy.
# Sources: Wikipedia read as raw text and its Spokane County Register list; the National Register record and form for
# the Holy Names Academy Building; the Cathedral of St. John's own page for its hours.
